// The arms industry the opening war is fought with.
//
// The seeding in the economy gives every region farms, workshops and roads from its people
// and how urban they are - and no arms industry at all, anywhere. For most of the world that
// is close enough: `national_arms_output` in common/production makes a share of GDP into
// weapons, and a country at peace needs little more. It is not close enough for a country
// that opens the game at war. Russia's nominal GDP makes about a sixth of what its field army
// burns at war, so it began the campaign with 40 % of the equipment it needed, and was still
// there half a year later - with the largest defence industry in Europe standing in the
// regions below. With the plants written in it opens at 98 %, and falls to about 90 % as the
// army grows, which is where buying from abroad starts to matter again.
//
// So the plants are written down where they are. Each one is the building of the same name
// in common/buildings - 4.5 Arms a week when fully staffed, by the `arms_industry` recipe in
// common/production - and each is a real cluster rather than a single factory:
//
//   Sverdlovsk     Uralvagonzavod in Nizhny Tagil, Uraltransmash - tanks and self-propelled guns
//   Udmurtia       Kalashnikov in Izhevsk, the Votkinsk missile plant
//   Tula           KBP, Splav, Tulamashzavod - guided weapons and rocket artillery
//   Moscow         Almaz-Antey, Tactical Missiles Corporation, the aviation design bureaux
//   Nizhny Novgorod  Arzamas, the Sverdlov explosives works in Dzerzhinsk
//   Tatarstan      Kazan helicopters, the Alabuga drone works
//   Kurgan         Kurganmashzavod - infantry fighting vehicles
//   Perm           Motovilikha - artillery and rocket launchers; the Perm powder works
//   Omsk           Omsktransmash - tanks
//   Vladimir       Degtyarev in Kovrov - small arms, anti-tank weapons, drones
//
//   Kyiv           Artem, Antonov, Kuznya na Rybalskomu
//   Dnipropetrovsk Pivdenmash, the Pavlohrad chemical plant
//
// Ukraine's industry is smaller and the rest of what it fights with is bought or given, which
// the trade pass already covers. A later file naming the same region wins, as everywhere else
// in history/: a mod that disagrees with a number changes that one region and inherits the rest.
{
  "ru_sve": { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 2 } },
  "ru_ud":  { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ru_tul": { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ru_mow": { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ru_niz": { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ru_ta":  { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ru_kgn": { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ru_per": { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ru_oms": { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ru_vla": { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },

  "ua_32":  { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } },
  "ua_12":  { "buildings": { "ArmsIndustry": 1 } }
}
